# Internal files → the homepage
#
# Pages serves every file in the repo root, so docs, scripts, SQL and
# worker source kept here for the people working on the site were
# readable by anyone. These rules send those paths to / instead.
#
# Cloudflare applies _redirects even when a file exists at the path,
# which is what makes this work. They do NOT apply to Function routes,
# so /CLAUDE.md and /README.md are handled by functions/CLAUDE.md.js
# and functions/README.md.js (404), not here.
#
# Adding a new doc, script or patch at the root? Add its path below.
# Splats are only used for whole folders (the one place Cloudflare
# documents them); root files are listed by name.
#
# 302, not 301, so this stays undoable by editing this file.

# ---- Folders that are not part of the site ----
/tools/*              /  302
/scripts/*            /  302
/migrations/*         /  302
/worker/*             /  302
/worker-picks-cron/*  /  302
/dlstreams-worker/*   /  302
/replacement/*        /  302

